31: /// Derive the identity_id from a hex-encoded Ed25519 public key.
32: ///
33: /// This is the single source of truth for the public_key -> identity_id
34: /// derivation, so callers outside this module never reimplement the hash.
35: /// Returns `None` when the input is not a valid Ed25519 public key: the
36: /// relation is one-way, so an identity_id can never be reversed back into a
37: /// public key, and hashing an arbitrary 64-hex string (e.g. an identity_id
38: /// itself, double-hashing) must not be allowed.
39: pub fn identity_id_from_public_key_hex(public_key_hex: &str) -> Option<String> {
40:     // `is_valid_public_key` checks the 64-hex form AND that the decoded bytes
